// Blocks ways that OSM's conditional tags close to motor vehicles on the day
// the graph was built. Applied to car, car4wd, carnotoll and motorcycle.
//
// GraphHopper 9.0 took conditional restrictions out of `car_access` and put
// them in `car_temporal_access`, so `access:conditional=no @ (Nov 1-Apr 15)`
// stopped closing anything by itself. This file is the restoration upstream
// documents for that change (docs/migration/config-migration-08-09.md).
//
// The condition is evaluated at import, not per request:
// OSMTemporalAccessParser resolves it against `date_range_parser_day`, which
// defaults to the import date. Since a new extract triggers a fresh import, the
// answer is never more than a day or so stale, and that is the whole mechanism
// -- there is no query-time date and no way to ask for a different one.
//
// Blocked rather than surfaced. A seasonal closure is a closure, and a route
// through one is wrong however it is styled; and 11.0 has no
// `access_conditional` path detail to style it with anyway -- only this enum.
//
// One file per vehicle because the encoded value has to match: a winter closure
// for cars must not stop anyone walking. `motorcycle` reads the car value since
// there is no motorcycle-specific one, and CarTemporalAccess.CONDITIONALS
// covers access/vehicle/motor_vehicle/motorcar -- only the last of those is
// strictly not a motorcycle.
//
// The permissive direction is read too, and that is this file's sharp edge.
// getTemporaryAccess returns the range check itself for a `yes @ (...)` value, so
// a way tagged only `motor_vehicle:conditional=yes @ (May-Oct)`, with nothing
// closing it the rest of the year, comes out NO in January -- and the rule below
// then makes it unroutable all winter. That reading is right where the
// conditional is the only thing granting access and wrong where it merely
// restates a default. Rare, but it is the one case where this file blocks
// something OSM does not say is closed.
//
// Covers dates and seasons only. DateRangeParser rejects a time-of-day rule
// like `no @ (Mo-Fr 08:00-18:00)`, which leaves the value MISSING, and any
// value containing `;` is skipped outright. Opening hours are not modelled.
//
// `car_temporal_access` must stay in `graph.encoded_values`: prepareImport
// aborts with "Encoded values missing" when a custom model names one that the
// config does not list.
{
  "priority": [
    { "if": "car_temporal_access == NO", "multiply_by": "0" }
  ]
}
